3. What Was the Actual Error?
The important error was:

x509: certificate has expired or is not yet valid

The image being pulled was:

docker-releases.dot-portal.de.pri.o2.com/docker:19.03.12-dind

The failure happened during:

prepare environment

because the Kubernetes executor was trying to pull the required image.

4. What Is Docker-in-Docker?
The image was:

docker:19.03.12-dind

DinD means Docker-in-Docker.

In CI/CD environments, DinD can be used when a pipeline needs to build Docker images inside a CI job.

You can explain:

“The GitLab runner was using a Docker-in-Docker image as part of the CI environment. Before the job could execute, the Kubernetes executor had to pull that image from our private Docker registry.”

So the application code itself wasn't necessarily broken.

The pipeline infrastructure failed before the actual job could start.

That's an important point.

