That's technically precise.

6. Why Didn't Docker Just Ignore the Certificate?
Very likely question.

Answer:

“Docker uses HTTPS when communicating with the registry. TLS certificate validation is part of establishing the secure connection. Since the certificate was expired, the client rejected the connection instead of pulling the image.”

Don't suggest disabling certificate validation.

You can explicitly say:

“Disabling TLS verification would not be an appropriate production fix because it would weaken the security of the registry connection.”

Excellent security point.

7. What Was the Root Cause?
This is the key RCA.

Root cause:
“The certificate had been renewed, but the renewed certificate was not attached to the load balancer serving the Nexus subdomains and external vendor endpoints.”

