This is different from saying:

“We forgot to renew the certificate.”

The certificate was renewed.

The actual problem was incomplete deployment/attachment of the renewed certificate.

8. Five Whys
This incident is perfect for explaining the 5 Whys methodology.

Why 1 — Why did GitLab pipelines fail?
Because the Kubernetes runner could not pull the required Docker image.

Why 2 — Why couldn't the image be pulled?
Because the HTTPS/TLS connection to the private Docker registry failed certificate validation.

Why 3 — Why did certificate validation fail?
Because the registry endpoint was presenting an expired certificate.

Why 4 — Why was an expired certificate still being presented?
Because the renewed certificate had not been attached to the load balancer serving the Nexus subdomains and external vendor endpoints.

Why 5 — Why wasn't this caught during certificate renewal?
Because the certificate renewal checklist did not explicitly verify certificate attachment across all associated load balancers and endpoints, and there was no proactive SSL certificate expiry monitoring for these endpoints.

This is the real root-cause story.

