37. Strong Troubleshooting Answer
If asked:

“How would you troubleshoot an ImagePullBackOff?”

Give this structured answer:

“First I would run kubectl describe pod and inspect the Events section to understand why the image pull failed.

Then I would classify the failure—whether it is authentication, image-not-found, network connectivity, DNS, TLS certificate validation, or registry availability.

For an x509 error, I would check the registry endpoint's TLS certificate using tools such as curl or openssl s_client. I would verify the certificate validity period, hostname, issuer, and certificate chain.

If the registry is behind a load balancer, I would then verify which certificate is attached to the listener and whether the endpoint is actually serving the renewed certificate.

Finally, after correcting the issue, I would validate the registry endpoint, perform an image pull, and rerun the pipeline.”

That answer is very interview-ready.

